\title{decomposer: Generic Decomposition Framework for Discrete-Time Simulations}
\description{
A model-agnostic decomposition framework that attributes changes in simulation outcomes to individual input factors using Shapley value decomposition. Any calibrated discrete-time simulation model can use the decomposer by implementing a small set of S3 methods: run the model, summarize outputs, and construct counterfactual inputs. Supports two counterfactual types: "change_since" (hold factor at baseline-year value) and "total_impact" (set factor to zero).
